# Committed unified-diff patches for NXP vendor sources. A context line for
# tab-indented vendor code necessarily begins "<space><tab>" (the diff's
# context marker followed by the original tab indentation), which
# `git diff --check` reports as "space before tab". That is structural to the
# diff format, not a real defect, and the context bytes must stay faithful to
# the upstream file for `patch` to apply. Exempt these files from whitespace
# checking so the signal stays meaningful.
*.patch -whitespace
